decision_conditions:
Condition : 32 - No development shall take place until a Construction Environmental Management Plan (CEMP) covering both the demolition and construction stages has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CEMP shall cover:

(a) Any external illumination of the site;
(b) Measures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site;
(c) Measures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties;
(d) The routeing of vehicles to the site, access and egress arrangements and waiting areas;
(e) Boundary treatment and measures to ensure they are maintained in a secure and tidy condition; and
(f) Considerate Contractor Scheme.


The development shall be implemented in accordance with the approved details.
